[13.958591, "o", "I'll take a look at your Python/pip setup to see what's going on.\r\n"]
[13.991428, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mecho \"USER: $(id -un) UID: $(id -u)\"; echo \"--- python paths ---\"; python3 -c \"import sys; print(sys.executable); print(sys.prefix); print(sys.path)\" 2>&1\r\nUSER: root UID: 0\r\n--- python paths ---\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3\r\n/usr/local\r\n['', '/usr/local/lib/python313.zip', '/usr/local/lib/python3.13', '/usr/local/lib/python3.13/lib-dynload', '/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages']\r\n"]
[14.062595, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mwhich -a python python3 pip pip3 2>&1; echo \"--- versions ---\"; python3 --version 2>&1; pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n/usr/local/bin/python\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3\r\n/usr/bin/python3\r\n/bin/python3\r\n/usr/local/bin/pip\r\n/usr/local/bin/pip3\r\n--- versions ---\r\nPython 3.13.1\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/local/bin/pip3\", line 5, in <module>\r\n    from pip._internal.cli.main import main\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\r\n"]
[15.018791, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[15.807963, "o", "Found the core problem. Let me dig a bit deeper before fixing.\r\n"]
[15.817026, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ 2>&1 | head -50\r\ntotal 24\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Oct 31 13:45 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Jan 14  2025 ..\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  119 Jan 14  2025 README.txt\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jan 14  2025 pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\n"]
[16.003808, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mecho \"--- pip script ---\"; cat /usr/local/bin/pip3 2>&1; echo \"--- ensurepip ---\"; python3 -m ensurepip --version 2>&1\r\n--- pip script ---\r\n#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13\r\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\r\nimport re\r\nimport sys\r\nfrom pip._internal.cli.main import main\r\nif __name__ == '__main__':\r\n    sys.argv[0] = re.sub(r'(-script\\.pyw|\\.exe)?$', '', sys.argv[0])\r\n    sys.exit(main())\r\n--- ensurepip ---\r\npip 24.3.1\r\n"]
[16.864078, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[18.859745, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/ 2>&1; echo \"--- is pip pkg dir present? ---\"; ls -d /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip 2>&1\r\ntotal 1792\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root    4096 Jan 14  2025 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root    4096 Jan 14  2025 ..\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1822182 Jan 14  2025 pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\n--- is pip pkg dir present? ---\r\nls: cannot access '/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip': No such file or directory\r\n"]
[18.911327, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mpython3 -c \"import ensurepip, os; print(os.path.dirname(ensurepip.__file__))\" 2>&1; echo \"--- dist-info contents ---\"; ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info/ 2>&1\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip\r\n--- dist-info contents ---\r\ntotal 112\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root  4096 Jan 14  2025 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  4096 Oct 31 13:45 ..\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 10925 Jan 14  2025 AUTHORS.txt\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root     4 Jan 14  2025 INSTALLER\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  1093 Jan 14  2025 LICENSE.txt\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  3677 Jan 14  2025 METADATA\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 65525 Jan 14  2025 RECORD\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root     0 Jan 14  2025 REQUESTED\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root    91 Jan 14  2025 WHEEL\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root    87 Jan 14  2025 entry_points.txt\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root     4 Jan 14  2025 top_level.txt\r\n"]
[20.1693, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[30.549285, "o", "Diagnosis is clear. Let me confirm one more thing and then fix it.\r\n"]
[30.579701, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED 2>&1; echo \"--- other python ---\"; /usr/bin/python3 --version 2>&1; /usr/bin/python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 | head -3\r\nls: cannot access '/usr/local/lib/python3.13/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED': No such file or directory\r\n--- other python ---\r\nPython 3.11.2\r\n/usr/bin/python3: No module named pip\r\n"]
[31.421381, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[32.441822, "o", "The problem is isolated: your `python3` (3.13.1 at `/usr/local/bin`) has pip's metadata but the actual `pip/` package folder was deleted. Let me restore it from the copy bundled with Python.\r\n"]
[33.869712, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mWHEEL=/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\npython3 - \"$WHEEL\" <<'PY'\r\nimport sys, runpy\r\nwhl = sys.argv[1]\r\nsys.path.insert(0, whl)          # import pip from the bundled wheel\r\nsys.argv = [\"pip\", \"install\", \"--no-index\", \"--no-cache-dir\", \"--force-reinstall\", whl]\r\nrunpy.run_module(\"pip\", run_name=\"__main__\")\r\nPY\r\nProcessing /usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\nInstalling collected packages: pip\r\n  Attempting uninstall: pip\r\n    Found existing installation: pip 24.3.1\r\n    Uninstalling pip-24.3.1:\r\n      Successfully uninstalled pip-24.3.1\r\nSuccessfully installed pip-24.3.1\r\nWARNING: Running pip as the 'root' user can result in broken permissions and conflicting behaviour with the system package manager, possibly rendering your system unusable.It is recommended to use a virtual environment instead: https://pip.pypa.io/warnings/venv. Use the --root-user-action option if you know what you are doing and want to suppress this war"]
[33.869774, "o", "ning.\r\n"]
[34.830923, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[35.30621, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mls -d /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip 2>&1; python3 -c \"import pip; print('import OK:', pip.__version__)\" 2>&1\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip\r\nimport OK: 24.3.1\r\n"]
[35.616369, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mpip --version 2>&1; pip3 --version 2>&1; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n"]
[36.437881, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[37.51991, "o", "Now verifying pip can actually resolve and install:\r\n"]
[37.681917, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mpip list 2>&1 | head -20\r\nPackage Version\r\n------- -------\r\npip     24.3.1\r\n"]
[37.945472, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mtimeout 60 pip install --dry-run --no-cache-dir --quiet six 2>&1 | tail -20; echo \"exit: $?\"\r\n[notice] A new release of pip is available: 24.3.1 -> 26.2.2\r\n[notice] To update, run: pip install --upgrade pip\r\nexit: 0\r\n"]
[39.02041, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[42.854954, "o", "Fixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did.\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\nYour `python3` is Python 3.13.1 at `/usr/local/bin/python3`. In its site-packages, the `pip` metadata still existed but the actual package code was gone:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/\r\n├── pip-24.3.1.dist-info/   ← metadata present\r\n└── (pip/ directory missing) ← code deleted\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `pip`/`pip3` launcher scripts at `/usr/local/bin` are still intact, but they start with `from pip._internal.cli.main import main`, so every invocation died with:\r\n\r\n```\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is a partial deletion — something removed the `pip/` folder while leaving the `.dist-info` behind (an interrupted uninstall, a stray `rm -rf`, or a tool cleaning site-packages). It wasn't a permissions or PATH issue, and before I fixed it, `pip install` would fail before it ever reached the network.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nI reinstalled pip from the wheel that ships with your Python installation (`ensurepip`'s bund"]
[42.854993, "o", "led `pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`) using `--force-reinstall`, which replaced the orphaned install cleanly:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSuccessfully uninstalled pip-24.3.1\r\nSuccessfully installed pip-24.3.1\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ pip --version\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n\r\n$ python3 -m pip --version\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n\r\n$ pip list\r\nPackage Version\r\n------- -------\r\npip     24.3.1\r\n```\r\n\r\nI also ran `pip install --dry-run six`, which resolved the package successfully — so installs work end to end.\r\n\r\n## Two things worth knowing\r\n\r\n- There's a **second Python** at `/usr/bin/python3` (Debian 3.11.2) that has **no pip at all**. Your `python3` resolves to the `/usr/local` one, so you're fine, but if you ever call `/usr/bin/python3 -m pip` directly it will still say \"No module named pip\".\r\n- `pip list` shows only pip installed. That's normal for this Python 3.13 build (no `setuptools`/`wheel`), and pip can bootstrap tho"]
[42.855001, "o", "se when needed.\r\n\r\nSince this is a system-wide install, any future `pip install` will write into `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages` as root and can affect the whole system — a virtualenv (`python3 -m venv myenv`) is the safer route for project work. Optional: `pip install --upgrade pip` to move off 24.3.1 (26.2.2 is current).\r\n"]
